# wfg-log 1
# fixture mic - a mic cue through its rack channel: heard, stopped, fired again, its
# plugin's child killed, and a double Esc (namespace draft 18.5, stage 9b.5, 2026-09-26).
#
# WHAT IT IS FOR: that a mic cue's life replays from the document and the log alone,
# with no interface and no child. GO claims Vox 1 and arms on its track - audio.armed is
# the audio side's word, re-injected - and the run starts; Esc ends it only when its
# tail has rung out, run.ended fourteen ticks after run.stopAll: the five-millisecond
# shut, then a quarter of a second of quiet at the channel's output stage. Fired again,
# the cue takes the channel again; its plugin's child dies from its own parameter and
# the failure says which channel plays without it; and a double Esc ends the run at
# once. Recorded from a real `wfg serve --hosted --input-wav` of a copy of
# tests/fixtures/bundles/mic fed a steady level at its first input, driven over OSC by
# tests/blackbox/phase9b_mic.py --keep-log.
#
# bundle mic sha256:302b8a997a4df022ebf7df01b8d14ee86b55e40406dd34282adb042c29043e57
